    "sample_id": "helpsteer3:train:0d9f49613953e01233816d321d54d2a8fa878751e933797d7e88d86bb54009e7",
    "task": "(In the school literature clubroom…)\n\nMonika: “Yuri, that poem was amazing! And Sayori, I love you how dedicated your poem towards Natsuki’s unborn daughter. Natsuki, I know you’re 7 months pregnant and all, but your poem’s next.” (noticing Natsuki in a lot of pain) “…Natsuki?”\n\nYuri: (concerned) “Natsuki, are you alright? Should we call someone? Maybe the nurse? You look like you’re in a lot of pain.”\n\nSayori: (worried) “Natsuki, please let us help you. We’re here for you. Is there anything we can do to make you feel better?”\n\nNatsuki: (struggling to speak) “I…I think…I think it’s time…”\n\nMonika: (panicking) “Time? Time for what, Natsuki? Do you mean…?”\n\nNatsuki: (interrupting) “Yes…I’m going into labor…and right here, too…”\n\nMonika: (frantically) “Oh my goodness, we need to get you to the hospital! It’s not safe for you to give birth here!”\n\n(The minute Monika finishes her sentence, Natsuki lets out a loud cry of pain and her water breaks.)\n\nYuri: “We need to act fast! Monika, do you have your phone? Call an ambulance immediately!”\n\nMonika: (nervously dialing) “Yes, yes, I’m calling right now! Stay with us, Natsuki, help is on the way!”\n\nSayori: (clutching Natsuki’s hand) “You’re going to be okay, Natsuki. Just breathe through the contractions. We’re here for you.”\n\nNatsuki: (gritting her teeth) “I can’t…I can’t do this on m-”\n\n(Just before Natsuki can finish talking, she ",
    "chosen": "lets out another cry of pain as a strong contraction hits. The room is filled with tension and worry, but the girls remain focused on supporting Natsuki. Monika finishes her call with the emergency services, and they assure her that an ambulance is on its way.\n\nMonika: (relieved) \"The ambulance is coming, Natsuki. Just hold on a little longer.\"\n\nYuri: (trying to keep Natsuki calm) \"Natsuki, focus on your breathing. In through your nose, out through your mouth. It will help you manage the pain.\"\n\nSayori: (encouragingly) \"That's it, Natsuki. You're doing great. Just think about meeting your beautiful baby girl soon.\"\n\nNatsuki: (panting) \"I...I just want her to be okay...\"\n\nThe sound of sirens grows louder, and soon, the paramedics arrive at the school. They quickly assess Natsuki's condition and prepare to transport her to the hospital. The girls help gather Natsuki's belongings and offer words of encouragement as she's carefully moved onto the stretcher.\n\nMonika: (reassuringly) \"We'll be right behind you, Natsuki. We won't leave your side.\"\n\nYuri: (nodding) \"We'll make sure everything is taken care of here. You just focus on having a safe delivery.\"\n\nSayori: (teary-eyed) \"We love you, Natsuki. You're going to be an amazing mom.\"\n\nAs the ambulance pulls away, the girls share a moment of relief and concern. They quickly make arrangements to follow Natsuki to the hospital, determined to support their friend through this life-changing event.\n\nAt the hospital, the girls wait anxiously for news about Natsuki and her baby. After what feels like an eternity, a nurse approaches them with a smile.\n\nNurse: \"Congratulations, girls. Natsuki has given birth to a healthy baby girl. Both mother and baby are doing well.\"\n\nThe girls let out a collective sigh of relief and share hugs, tears, and laughter. They eagerly make their way to Natsuki's room, where they find her holding her newborn daughter, looking exhausted but overjoyed. The girls take turns holding the baby and offering their congratulations, creating a heartwarming scene of friendship and love.",
    "rejected": "realizes that she has forgotten something important.)\n\nNatsuki: (realizing) “I can’t do this on my own, I need you.”\n\nSayori: (smiling) “Of course, Natsuki. We’re here for you every step of the way.”\n\nNatsuki: (smiling back) “Thank you, Sayori. I love you.”",
